{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuJdzRMh93ygqVHFpaac","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I created the dashboard and the alert rule. Both requests returned success. The rule is enabled, but it hasn't run yet (status \"pending\"), so I haven't seen it fire. I also didn't open the dashboard to check that the panels render.\n\n**1. What the data holds.** The `Kibana Sample Data Logs` data view has one document per web request, timed by the `timestamp` field. The useful fields are:\n- **Response:** `response`, the HTTP status code, stored as a string.\n- **Request:** `url`, `request` and `extension`.\n- **Size:** `bytes`.\n- **Client:** `clientip` and `agent`.\n- **Platform:** `machine.os` and `machine.ram`.\n- **Location:** `geo.src`, `geo.dest` and `geo.coordinates`.\n- **Other:** `referer`, `host` and `tags`.\n\n**2. Dashboard \"EFF-08b97b8c Web logs overview\"** (id `eff-08b97b8c-web-logs-overview-e83b29d70854`) has 7 panels:\n- **Single numbers:** total requests, unique visitors (distinct `clientip`), and total bytes served.\n- **Requests over time by response code:** a bar chart.\n- **Response code share:** a pie chart.\n- **Top 10 requested URLs:** a table with request count and bytes.\n- **Requests by operating system:** a bar chart.\n\nLink: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-08b97b8c-web-logs-overview-e83b29d70854\n\n**3. Alert rule \"EFF-08b97b8c 5xx spike\"** (id `5d1c226e-9857-4a9b-9151-e30e07aa1099`):\n- **Type:** an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`, timed by `timestamp`.\n- **Schedule:** checks every 1 minute.\n- **Condition:** fires when more than 10 matching requests arrive within the last 5 minutes.\n- **What counts as 5xx:** any request whose response code starts with \"5\" (`response.keyword` prefix `5`). Because the code is stored as text, this is a string match rather than a number range. I couldn't confirm the actual values because direct index queries are blocked here; standard 3-digit codes are assumed.\n- **Notifications:** the rule has no notification action attached, so it will record alerts but won't send them anywhere."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":551,"cache_read_input_tokens":21323,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":551},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0536cbf5-c97a-5467-80bd-e50c5d30a2ce","uuid":"59ba37b6-0966-4bd2-a9e4-d40c28939d9b","timestamp":"2026-10-10T21:57:44.957Z","request_id":"req_011CfuJdzGBYB6hLuU7Bxswk"}
